" Keep yanks, deletes and puts in sync with the system clipboard, matching
" the Neovim config's `clipboard = 'unnamedplus'`.
"
" This has to branch by platform. The "unnamedplus" flag uses the '+'
" register, which requires the +X11 or +wayland_clipboard feature. macOS vim
" ships +clipboard but no X11, so '+' is never wired to the pasteboard and
" "unnamedplus" silently does nothing there — only '*' works. Vim exposes
" has('unnamedplus') precisely for this test.
"
"   Linux (X11/Wayland) : unnamedplus,unnamed
"                         puts read CLIPBOARD, yanks also copy to PRIMARY
"   macOS               : unnamed
"                         the '*' register is the system pasteboard
if has('clipboard_working') || has('clipboard')
  if has('unnamedplus')
    set clipboard=unnamedplus,unnamed
  else
    set clipboard=unnamed
  endif
endif

" If yanks still do not reach the system clipboard, this vim was built
" without clipboard support. Check with:
"   vim --version | grep -o '[+-]clipboard'
" A '-clipboard' build needs a different package — on Debian the default vim
" is commonly built without it, and vim-gtk3 provides a build with +clipboard
" and +X11. Neovim is unaffected; it shells out to a clipboard provider.
